    {
      "name": "Approximation accuracy against exhaustive cosine",
      "rationale": "Exhaustive cosine over the whole corpus defines the exact answer, so this is the measure of how much the graph gives up for its speed. It is reported for rust-db only: the same question cannot be asked of pgvector without reading its index internals, and pgvector's own accuracy against exact search is a property of the same HNSW algorithm at the same parameters. A figure well below what HNSW should reach at m = 16 and ef_construction = 64 would indicate a graph defect rather than a tuning choice.",
      "rows": [
        {
          "label": "all sources, no predicate (180 queries)",
          "metric": "recall@10",
          "measures": [
            {
              "engine": "rust-db",
              "value": 0.9027774333953857
